{"id": "EUVD-2026-102332", "enisaUuid": "0af002f8-d885-3a56-870f-5921c8c69ec4", "description": "pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a crontab injection vulnerability in interfaces_ppps_edit.php that allows authenticated users to execute commands as root by injecting newlines into the ptpid or reset hour/minute fields. Attackers holding the 'WebCfg - Interfaces: PPPs: Edit' privilege can submit crafted POST values that configure_cron() writes unescaped into /etc/crontab, running arbitrary root commands on schedule.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:49:22", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-pppoe-cron", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/interfaces.inc#L2174-L2214", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/interfaces_ppps_edit.php#L271-L278", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/services.inc#L5652-L5660", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-crontab-injection-via-ppp-periodic-reset-ptpid"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cx43-pf3x-hc6x", "CVE-2026-111220"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.73, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cd0af164-3f61-3e85-b015-9c8300a84dcc", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ed17d1a-5e93-3a0a-a8a4-52e278bd1e38", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}